dialect protocol
protocol stdio.las.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.las
start op
framing record

# Ticket 26/08/10/ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION: real binary op
# frame -- replaces both the pre-existing placeholder (`dialect protocol stdio.las.mutations` /
# `magic = %x00` / `payload = *OCTET`, pseudo-ABNF entirely outside this framework's real
# `.protocol.semio` dialect) AND the F6 `print_las_mutation(self).into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut this artifact's `OpBinary::encode_op` used to fall back to (see ../🦀️component.rs's
# upgraded `impl protocol::OpBinary for LasMutation`, `#region 🔖️BinaryOpCodec`). `LasMutation` is
# a 15-variant enum, none of them a self-recursive/data-carrying value type (unlike json/csv's
# `JsonValue`/`CsvRecord`) -- but each variant's payload shape is genuinely DIFFERENT (some empty,
# some scalar tuples, some a whole nested `LasHeader`/`LasVlr`/`LasPoint` record), and this
# dialect's `repeat`/`arm` tag-dispatch construct exists only for a REPEATED sequence of records,
# not a single one-shot "read a tag byte, then branch into one of 15 differently-shaped payloads"
# read -- the same `protocol-array-of-records`-adjacent gap zip/binary's own already-real mutations
# protocols hit (`💾️binary/…/🧬️mutations/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio`'s own doc comment
# names this exact limitation for its `dsl::variants_binary`-routed `ordinal`). The two REAL fixed
# leading fields (`format`, the variant `tag`) ARE protocol-walkable and modeled here field-by-
# field; the variant-specific payload tail stays one opaque trailing chain -- the Rust
# `encode_op`/`decode_op` side (same file, `#region 🔖️BinaryOpCodec`) IS genuinely, fully
# structured, real per-variant binary all the way down (round-trip tested by
# `op_text_binary_roundtrip_law`), this protocol file honestly bounds only what it can
# field-by-field walk.

field format u8
field tag u8
chain body bytes
